%% section: Services
%% caption: How a request reaches a pod
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client pod
    participant DNS as CoreDNS
    participant PX as kube-proxy rules
    participant P as Backend pod
    C->>DNS: resolve my-svc.my-ns.svc.cluster.local
    DNS-->>C: the Service's ClusterIP — a virtual IP, nothing listens on it
    C->>PX: packet to ClusterIP
    PX->>PX: iptables or IPVS rule rewrites the destination
    PX->>P: DNAT to a ready pod IP
    P-->>C: response
    Note over PX: the rule set comes from EndpointSlices, which come from readiness
    Note over C,P: headless Service returns pod IPs directly instead — that is how StatefulSets are addressed
